<title>GERMANY: East German Nov industry orders rise 5.6 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>East German Nov industry orders rise 5.6 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Nov 96     Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +5.6	 -3.7(3.0)   +20.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     -21.8	-11.0(10.3)    n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		132.7	125.7(126.6) 169.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  Nov 96    Oct 96    Nov 96 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     +2.8	-2.9     151.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Aug/Sept 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  -2.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Oct/Nov 95:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		 -17.2</p>
<p> Domestic orders			-20.4</p>
<p> Foreign orders			  +2.1</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +12.7</p>
<p> Capital goods			  -44.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    -2.7</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
